.DS_Store
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/sdks
!.yarn/versions
node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo
.build/

dsh-plugin-desktop/dist/
dsh-plugin-desktop/lib/
dsh-community-market/lib/

.env.yarn
# Teacher DSH layer
teacher/**/node_modules/
teacher/**/dist/
# `@teacher-dsh/global-memory` compiles to JavaScript; its output is rebuilt by
# build-teacher-runtime.mjs, so it is not tracked — matching the sibling teacher packages, which
# carry no build output at all.
teacher/packages/*/lib/
# Recorded eval sessions: `record.mjs` writes a throwaway DSH home per case, and a real run's log
# is an artifact of that machine's provider, not repository content.
teacher/evals/**/.runs/
teacher/**/*.tgz
teacher/legacy/node_modules/

# Teacher DSH build outputs. Everything below is produced by scripts/teacher/*.mjs from the
# pinned inputs in teacher/ and resources/teacher-seed/plugins, and is staged into the installer
# by electron-builder's extraResources. Never commit it.
build/
resources/dsh-runtime/
resources/teacher-runtime/
resources/teacher-seed/plugins-built/

# NOTE: licenses/ is intentionally NOT ignored. It holds the verbatim license text of every
# dependency the installer bundles (about 2.7 MB), and a public distribution must ship those
# texts alongside the code - in particular the CC BY-SA 4.0 Education Agent Skills.

# Throwaway probes and scratch scripts must never be committed.
/tmp-*
/tmp_*
dsh-plugin-desktop/dist-release/
